<title>INDIA: Indian silver down on profit-taking, gold steady.</title>
<headline>Indian silver down on profit-taking, gold steady.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Silver prices closed lower on profit-taking on Thursday after opening on a subdued note while gold held steady, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Demand resistance by industrial consumers affected market sentiment,&quot; said a dealer. Silver rose 120 rupees per kg in the last two days.</p>
<p>Gold held steady in a narrow trading range in limited activity. Seasonal buying was low but scattered supplies kept the market quiet.</p>
<p>Gold biscuits (116.50 grammes each) were unchanged at 60,450 rupees. They rose by 150 rupees on Wednesday.</p>
